In an ICAO flight plan, planned cruising speed is expressed as True Airspeed in terms of:

Kilometres per hour, expressed as K followed by 4 figures (e.g. K0830); 
or Knots, expressed as N followed by 4 figures (e.g. N0485); 
or Mach Number, when so prescribed by the appropriate ATS authority, to the nearest hundredth of unit Mach, expressed as M followed by 3 figures (e.g. M082).

[Source: 7-Flight-Planning-and-Monitoring-2014.pdf, Page 237]
